This product includes software developed by third parties. A release archive
carries two documents generated from the locked dependency graph (Cargo.lock):

  THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt   the license and notice files that each bundled
                             package carries, package by package
  sbom.cdx.json              a CycloneDX bill of materials: every package with
                             its version, license expression, crate checksum
                             and dependency edges

Notable bundled components, all under permissive licenses:

  SQLite                     public domain; compiled in through the bundled
                             feature of rusqlite
  tree-sitter and the        MIT; the Python, JavaScript, TypeScript, Rust, C
  tree-sitter grammars       and C++ grammars are compiled into the binary
  rust-protobuf              MIT; reads SCIP indexes
  rmcp and Tokio             Apache-2.0 and MIT; the local stdio MCP server
  serde, serde_json          MIT OR Apache-2.0

The Rust toolchain (rustc/cargo/rustfmt/clippy) is used at build time only and
is not redistributed. Language servers and SCIP indexers that an operator
chooses to run (clangd, rust-analyzer, scip-typescript) are separate programs
under their own licenses; Riltra does not bundle or install them.

The package set is pinned in Cargo.lock; the audit table with versions,
licenses and origins is docs/licensing.md. The release workflow fails when the
committed SBOM no longer matches Cargo.lock (release/README.md).
